From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thibaut Lapierre <root@epheo.eu>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:50:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 14/18] apiserver: structured authentication config

apiServer.authenticationConfig names a structured authentication
configuration file that kube-apiserver takes as --authentication-config:
JWT issuers, audiences and claim mappings, a site's OIDC provider for
instance. Client certificates and ServiceAccount tokens keep working
beside it, and kube-apiserver reloads the file when it changes. A config.d
drop-in can set it, so a site layer ships a file and a drop-in, no code.

The path must be absolute. The kube-apiserver controller fails the start
naming the setting when the file is missing. The file must not configure
anonymous authentication: MicroShift sets --anonymous-auth.

Upstream: no authentication setting as of 5.0.
Covered by: config unit tests; vm-test (a token from an HTTPS issuer pod
authenticates with a prefixed username and mapped groups, a file edit
applies without a restart, the apiserver starts with the issuer down).
